-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 66: define the `mentions` edge table as a proper
--   TYPE RELATION FROM source TO entity
-- so the document↔entity bipartite graph (Track U.2) can be RELATEd, traversed,
-- drawn and exported.
--
-- Background. The ontology (schema_core.yaml) defines a `MENTIONS`
-- relationship (CreativeWork → Person/Org/Place/Event/Thing). On staging the
-- physical `mentions` table was auto-created as the SurrealDB default
--   DEFINE TABLE mentions TYPE ANY SCHEMALESS
-- (verified via INFO FOR DB on 2026-06-27), NOT a relation table — so
-- `RELATE source -> mentions -> entity` would store an untyped record rather
-- than a graph edge, and the table holds 0 rows. The sibling edge tables
-- (`cites`, `discusses`, `authored_by`) are already correct
-- `TYPE RELATION IN source OUT ...`; `mentions` is the one that drifted.
--
-- Strategy (mirrors migration 62's non-destructive remediation of `relation`):
--   1. DELETE only null-endpoint junk rows (in = NONE OR out = NONE). A real
--      `mentions` edge always has non-null in/out, so this is a no-op on a
--      healthy table and only clears the non-edge junk a drifted TYPE ANY table
--      could hold (which would otherwise block the RELATION redefine). A blanket
--      `DELETE mentions` would WIPE healthy edges — exactly the destructive
--      mistake migration 58 made for `relation`; 62 fixed it with this
--      null-endpoint-only predicate and 66 follows suit.
--   2. DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE ... TYPE RELATION FROM source TO entity. On
--      SurrealDB >= 2.1.4 (staging runs v2) OVERWRITE converts the drifted
--      TYPE ANY table to a RELATION table; on an already-correct RELATION table
--      OVERWRITE re-asserts the identical definition and PRESERVES existing edge
--      records (the empirical fact migration 62 established and its container
--      test proves), so it is a safe no-op for healthy edges.
--   3. DEFINE the edge fields with OVERWRITE. `weight` is the U.2 projection
--      weight (R.2 salience × rarity); the rest mirror the `relation` provenance
--      shape (migration 39) so the materialized layer is uniform.
--
-- Strict-field / S.4 note. Every strict field below carries a DEFAULT, and the
-- table is EMPTY (0 rows on staging; the regenerator clears+recreates anyway),
-- so there are NO pre-existing rows to drift — no backfill UPDATE is required
-- (the drift-only-WHERE coalesce of migration 65 applies to tables that already
-- hold rows; `mentions` does not). `mentions` rows are only ever written by the
-- U.2 regenerator via RELATE-with-SET, which supplies `weight`/`concept_*`
-- explicitly, so the DEFAULTs are a safety floor, never the live value.
--
-- Idempotent + forward-only: the DELETE matches nothing on a second pass and
-- every OVERWRITE re-asserts an identical definition. Down is a documented
-- no-op (a schema repair has no faithful inverse; reverting to TYPE ANY would
-- re-break RELATE — the very drift this fixes).
-- ============================================================================

-- 1. Drop ONLY null-endpoint junk rows (the non-edge records a drifted TYPE ANY
--    table could hold). Real `mentions` edges always have non-null in/out, so
--    this never touches them — no-op on the empty staging table AND on any
--    healthy edge set.
DELETE mentions WHERE in = NONE OR out = NONE;

-- 2. Re-assert the canonical edge definition. Converts a drifted TYPE ANY table
--    to RELATION on v2; identical no-op (edges preserved) on an already-correct
--    RELATION table.
DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE mentions SCHEMAFULL TYPE RELATION FROM source TO entity;

-- 3. Edge fields. `weight` is the U.2 projection weight (R.2 salience × rarity);
--    `concept_name` / `concept_type` / `document_frequency` carry the per-edge
--    "why" (the shared concept that drove the link, for the viz + export). The
--    provenance fields mirror migration 39's `relation` shape so the
--    materialized layer is uniform and the regenerator can be reasoned about
--    the same way.
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE weight ON mentions TYPE float DEFAULT 0.0;
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE concept_name ON mentions TYPE string DEFAULT "";
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE concept_type ON mentions TYPE string DEFAULT "";
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE document_frequency ON mentions TYPE int DEFAULT 0;

DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE projection_method ON mentions TYPE string DEFAULT "source_documents";
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE created_at ON mentions TYPE datetime DEFAULT time::now();

-- Indexes (OVERWRITE so a re-apply or a legacy index set converges).
DEFINE INDEX OVERWRITE idx_mentions_weight ON mentions FIELDS weight;
